{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-05 02:33:37 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-D-RotateLog] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] ATOMICITY ANALYSIS: Core rotation execution (lines 951-1008) uses rotate_file() utility which should handle file locking, but fallback path (lines 1021-1063) performs MANUAL rename + write operations WITHOUT explicit locking. This is a NON-ATOMIC write pattern. If fallback write_text() fails after rename, original log is moved but new file is empty/missing. [BUCKET:atomicity] [BUCKET:error_handling] [P0_CANDIDATE] | affected_code=[\"log_path.rename(archive_path)\", \"log_path.write_text(header)\"]; atomicity_violation=fallback_rotation_path; consequence=original_log_moved_but_new_file_missing; failure_mode=rename_succeeds_but_write_fails; lines=1021-1063; locking_present=False; p0_trigger=True; reasoning={\"how\": \"Code analysis of _execute_rotation_with_fallbacks lines 1021-1063 reveals manual file operations without locking or transaction semantics\", \"what\": \"Found non-atomic fallback path where rename and write are separate operations without transactional guarantees\", \"why\": \"Validating atomicity guarantees for rotation operations as specified in assignment\"}; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:33:37.609591+00:00_6343b2f0", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:33:37.609625+00:00"}
