{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:34:04 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-C-QueryEntries] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Discovered second sub-system: search query building (lines 406-584). Triple-layer validation continues here with parameter re-validation AFTER config object creation. Emergency fallback creates entire new QueryEntriesConfig on failure. Pattern: defense in depth or config object not trusted? | architectural_question=why_revalidate_after_config; lines_analyzed=406-800; observations=[\"re_validates_pagination_after_config\", \"emergency_fallback_creates_new_config_object\", \"hasattr_checks_for_optional_config_fields\"]; phase=structural_analysis; potential_bucket=[\"config\", \"error_handling\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced parameter flow: raw params \\u2192 healed \\u2192 config object \\u2192 extracted back \\u2192 re-validated \\u2192 mutated in search_params dict\", \"what\": \"Constraint: Config objects should encapsulate validation. Observation: Tool doesn't trust its own config object. Alternative: Config validation incomplete or parameters can mutate post-creation.\", \"why\": \"Need to understand why parameters are validated, then packaged into config, then validated again from config\"}; sub_system_identified=search_query_building; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:34:04.449356+00:00_f792fc29", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:34:04.449412+00:00"}
