{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:34:37 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-A-AppendEntry] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Creating wiki documentation structure. Identified 12 distinct sub-systems in append_entry.py: (1) Imports/Globals (1-75), (2) Vector Indexing Setup (77-94), (3) Sanitization Utilities (97-131), (4) ID Generation (134-168), (5) Parameter Validation/Healing (170-418), (6) Single Entry Processing (420-819), (7) Bulk Entry Processing (821-1137), (8) Mode Detection (1139-1167), (9) Main Function Orchestration (1232-1661), (10) Helper Delegation (1663-1755), (11) TEE Operations (1758-1840), (12) Parallel/Sequential Bulk Infrastructure (1842-2360). | extractable_modules_identified=8; reasoning={\"how\": \"Creating comprehensive wiki page with 8 required sections, tagging extractable modules with buckets, documenting implicit contracts (no project check, silent DB failures, vector non-blocking), preparing for token analysis.\", \"what\": \"Constraints: Document 12 distinct sub-systems with line ranges, flag extractable modules with bucket tags, identify implicit contracts and boundary violations. Found: Clear architectural seams at mode routing (single vs bulk), error handling layers (correct->heal->emergency), persistence operations (file->DB->vector).\", \"why\": \"Need to synthesize all findings into structured wiki documentation with clear sub-system boundaries for Phase 6 architect.\"}; sub_systems_count=12; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:34:37.909808+00:00_107a5f40", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:34:37.909843+00:00"}
