{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:34:45 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-C-QueryEntries] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Identified search scope routing architecture. Found 6 scopes (project/global/all_projects/research/bugs/all) with distinct behaviors. Key discovery: \"all_projects\" and \"research/bugs/all\" use SAME project iteration logic but different document type filtering. Scopes are NOT orthogonal variants - they're overlapping strategies with duplicated iteration code. | architectural_smell=duplicated_project_iteration; evidence=lines_1281_1297_and_1312_1330_nearly_identical; lines_analyzed=1271-1374; phase=architecture_mapping; potential_bucket=[\"search_strategy\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Compared routing branches, found code duplication in project iteration, different only in filtering predicate\", \"what\": \"Constraint: Each scope should have distinct purpose. Observation: 'all_projects' (lines 1279-1297) and 'research/bugs/all' (lines 1310-1340) iterate projects identically, only differing in _project_has_document_types filter.\", \"why\": \"Understanding scope routing reveals whether 6 scopes are architectural necessity or evolved duplication\"}; scope_count=6; scopes=[\"project\", \"global\", \"all_projects\", \"research\", \"bugs\", \"all\"]; sub_system=search_scope_routing; unification_opportunity=True; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:34:45.928863+00:00_bfbb1c4a", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:34:45.928899+00:00"}
