{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:35:43 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-C-QueryEntries] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Filter application analysis reveals non-composable sequential filter chain (lines 667-756). Found 10 filter types applied via imperative if-continue pattern: message, emoji, status-to-emoji mapping, agent, metadata, priority, category, confidence, time_range, relevance. Each filter is hard-coded inline with entry parsing logic. NOT composable - filters cannot be reordered, combined, or tested independently. Status filter bug on line 684-692: broken for-else logic means status filter inverted. | bug_description=for_else_logic_inverted_status_filter_broken; bug_found=True; bug_location=lines_684_692; composability=none; filter_count=10; filter_types=[\"message\", \"emoji\", \"status\", \"agent\", \"metadata\", \"priority\", \"category\", \"confidence\", \"time_range\", \"relevance\"]; lines_analyzed=660-780; pattern=imperative_sequential_chain; phase=filter_analysis; potential_bucket=[\"filtering\", \"validation\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced filter application flow, counted filter types, analyzed composability, identified control flow bug in status filter\", \"what\": \"Constraint: Filters should be composable predicates. Observation: 10 hard-coded filter types with if-continue pattern, cannot compose. Bug: Status filter for-else logic appears inverted (breaks when emoji NOT in status_emojis, then continues if no break).\", \"why\": \"Need to understand if filters are composable building blocks or monolithic implementation\"}; testability=low; unification_opportunity=True; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:35:43.583291+00:00_2585a026", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:35:43.583327+00:00"}
