{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-05 02:42:14 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-C-QueryEntries] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Completed token cost measurement for query_entries output formats. Measured 7 sample queries across readable/structured/compact formats. Key findings: Readable format averages 628 tokens with 56% structural overhead (boxes/separators). Compact format achieves 4.8x reduction (37 tokens/entry vs 173 for readable). Cross-project search adds 11% overhead. Empty results waste 51% on metadata. Structural tokens are biggest optimization opportunity. | avg_total_tokens=628; evidence_file=token_measurements_query_entries.json; formats=[\"readable\", \"structured\", \"compact\"]; max_tokens=1783; metadata_overhead=14%_avg; min_tokens=119; optimization_opportunities=[\"remove_boxes_in_compact\", \"cache_metadata_blocks\", \"omit_empty_filter_lists\"]; p95_tokens=1783; phase=token_measurement; reasoning={\"how\": \"Created sample outputs for each query pattern, used tiktoken cl100k_base encoding, categorized tokens as structural/metadata/content\", \"what\": \"Measured 7 diverse query patterns (empty, small, large, cross-project, with warnings). Constraint: Readable must remain human-friendly. Observation: Structural tokens (boxes) dominate readable format at 56%, compact achieves 4.8x reduction.\", \"why\": \"Need quantitative data on token costs to identify optimization opportunities and validate verbosity assumptions\"}; samples_measured=7; structural_overhead=30.2%_avg_56%_readable; tokens_per_entry={\"compact\": 37, \"readable\": 173, \"structured\": 134}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:42:14.437235+00:00_0b3238d0", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:42:14.437270+00:00"}
