{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:57:35 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] CRITICAL BUG-001 ANALYSIS VERIFICATION: Agent E's root cause is CORRECT but the proposed fix is FATALLY FLAWED. Verified actual code at line 459: `is_new = not progress_log_path.exists() or entry_count == 0`. The bug diagnosis is accurate - empty logs (post-rotation) incorrectly trigger new project SITREP. However, proposed fix (remove entry_count check, use only file.exists()) has a critical flaw: set_project line 667 calls generate_doc_templates which CREATES PROGRESS_LOG.md. On first call, file won't exist \u2192 templates generated \u2192 file.exists() becomes True \u2192 second call in same session would ALWAYS show existing SITREP even for truly new projects. Agent E missed the template generation side effect. | agent=E; bug_id=BUG-001; fatal_flaw=ignores_template_generation_side_effect; proposed_fix=flawed; root_cause=correct; severity=high; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:57:35.251575+00:00_f13852cb", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:57:35.251605+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-05T02:57:35.251575+00:00_f13852cb", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:57:35.263857+00:00"}
