{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:58:01 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] BUG-001 FLOW ANALYSIS: Tracing execution order in set_project.py. Line 246 calls _ensure_documents() which checks if docs exist (line 649). If PROGRESS_LOG.md doesn't exist, line 667 calls generate_doc_templates() to create it. THEN line 459 checks is_new = not progress_log_path.exists() or entry_count == 0. CRITICAL: On first call to brand new project, _ensure_documents CREATES the file, so by the time is_new check runs, file.exists() is ALWAYS True. This means Agent E's proposed fix (use only file.exists()) would work INCORRECTLY - first call would show existing SITREP because template was just created. Need to verify if _ensure_documents runs before or after is_new check. | analysis=execution_flow_trace; critical_question=does_ensure_documents_run_before_is_new_check; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:58:01.349185+00:00_d17b3f0b", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:01.349214+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-05T02:58:01.349185+00:00_d17b3f0b", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:01.360088+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 02:58:15 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] BUG-001 VERDICT: Agent E's root cause analysis is CORRECT, and the proposed fix is ACTUALLY CORRECT TOO. My initial concern was unfounded. Execution flow: (1) Line 246 _ensure_documents creates PROGRESS_LOG.md if missing, (2) Line 459 is_new check runs AFTER file creation. For new projects: file created with 0 entries \u2192 entry_count == 0 is True \u2192 is_new = True (correct). For rotated projects: file exists with 0 entries \u2192 entry_count == 0 is True \u2192 is_new = True (WRONG, should be False). Proposed fix 'is_new = not progress_log_path.exists()' works because: new project after _ensure_documents will have file.exists() = True AND entry_count = 0, so current buggy logic works by accident. Wait, this logic is confusing. Let me reconsider... | analysis=needs_deeper_verification; confusion=logic_still_unclear; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:58:15.661369+00:00_4b2e21e9", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:15.661401+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-05T02:58:15.661369+00:00_4b2e21e9", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:15.670996+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-05 02:58:31 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] CONFIRMED FATAL FLAW IN AGENT E'S FIX: Truth table analysis proves proposed fix breaks new project detection. Current buggy code works for new projects because entry_count == 0 catches newly created empty template. After _ensure_documents creates PROGRESS_LOG.md, file.exists() = True but entry_count = 0, so 'False or True = True' correctly identifies as new. Agent E's fix 'is_new = not file.exists()' would return False for brand new projects (file just created), showing existing SITREP instead of new SITREP. The CORRECT fix requires detecting template vs modified state, NOT just file existence. User's original analysis was spot-on: need hash comparison (baseline_hash vs current_hash) or database-tracked lifecycle state. | agent_e_grade_impact=major_deduction; bug_001_fix=incorrect; root_cause=correct; severity=critical; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T02:58:31.693582+00:00_de769025", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:31.693611+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-05T02:58:31.693582+00:00_de769025", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T02:58:31.703671+00:00"}
