{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-05 03:21:42 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-G-ListGetProjects] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] CRITICAL DISCOVERY: Complete hash retrieval data flow documented. ProjectRegistry.record_doc_update() (lines 187-282) stores baseline_hashes and current_hashes in meta.docs structure. get_project._compute_doc_status() (lines 28-40) extracts this data. Hash flow: (1) generate_doc_templates SHOULD call record_doc_update with template hash (2) Registry stores in meta.docs.baseline_hashes (3) get_project exposes via _compute_doc_status (4) Callers compare baseline==current to detect pristine templates. BUG-001 gap confirmed: generate_doc_templates NEVER calls record_doc_update. | data_flow_chain=[\"generate_doc_templates\", \"ProjectRegistry.record_doc_update\", \"meta.docs.baseline_hashes\", \"get_project._compute_doc_status\", \"caller_comparison\"]; integration_gap=generate_doc_templates missing record_doc_update call; phase=hash_architecture_complete; reasoning={\"how\": \"Examined ProjectRegistry.record_doc_update implementation (baseline_hashes map line 228, current_hashes map line 229, flag derivation lines 239-263) and get_project extraction (lines 28-40)\", \"what\": \"Full data flow traced: record_doc_update stores hashes in JSON meta field, get_project extracts and exposes, flags are auto-computed per doc (lines 239-263)\", \"why\": \"BUG-001 fix requires complete understanding of hash lifecycle from template creation through retrieval\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T03:21:42.010582+00:00_c1194367", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T03:21:42.010616+00:00"}
