{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 11:51:12 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase2-Storage] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Task 3 (PostgreSQL Backend) - Gap analysis complete. PostgreSQL has only 16 tables vs SQLite's 23 tables. MISSING TABLES: scribe_sessions, session_projects, agent_recent_projects, document_sections, custom_templates, document_changes, sync_status, agent_report_cards, reminder_history, tool_calls (10 tables missing, not 7). Also missing: FTS5 virtual table for document_sections_fts, and multiple indexes. PostgreSQL init.sql is 210 LOC vs sqlite.py schema setup 650-1060 LOC. delete_project method explicitly raises NotImplementedError at postgres.py:81-84. | critical_gaps=[\"scribe_sessions\", \"reminder_history\", \"tool_calls\", \"agent_report_cards\", \"document_sections\"]; file=storage/postgres.py; reasoning={\"how\": \"Line-by-line schema comparison, table counting, method implementation review in postgres.py\", \"what\": \"Compared PostgreSQL init.sql (16 tables, 210 LOC) against SQLite schema (23 tables, 400+ LOC), identified 10 missing tables and NotImplementedError for delete_project\", \"why\": \"Must document complete PostgreSQL gap analysis to inform implementation specs and feasibility assessment\"}; schema_file=db/init.sql; tables_missing=10; tables_postgres=16; tables_sqlite=23; task=task_3_postgres_audit; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T11:51:12.709638+00:00_72cecc15", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T11:51:12.709670+00:00"}
