{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-05 11:51:49 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase2-Storage] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Task 4 (Abstraction Violations) - CRITICAL violations identified. shared/project_registry.py has 9 direct sqlite3.connect() calls bypassing abstraction layer (lines 77, 94, 111, 177, 203, 284, 381, 436, 454). File manages project lifecycle state (648 LOC) but uses raw sqlite3 instead of StorageBackend interface. Also found: storage/sqlite.py internal usage (lines 1260, 2072 - acceptable as backend implementation), plugins/vector_indexer.py (line 331), shared/logging_utils.py (line 108), scripts/*.py (migration scripts). Tests appropriately use direct access for verification. NO asyncpg bypass found outside storage/postgres.py and db/*.py modules. | critical_file=shared/project_registry.py; file_loc=648; reasoning={\"how\": \"Grep search for sqlite3.connect and asyncpg imports, file-by-file analysis distinguishing production code from tests/backends, line number extraction\", \"what\": \"Identified 9 sqlite3.connect() calls in project_registry.py bypassing StorageBackend, plus 4 in other production files (vector_indexer, logging_utils, scripts)\", \"why\": \"Abstraction violations break PostgreSQL compatibility and create maintenance burden - must catalog all violations for enforcement spec\"}; task=task_4_abstraction_violations; violation_count=9; violation_lines=[77, 94, 111, 177, 203, 284, 381, 436, 454]; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T11:51:49.774488+00:00_84408330", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T11:51:49.774522+00:00"}
