{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 11:52:14 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase2-Storage] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Task 5 (Data Models) - models.py analyzed. Defines 13 dataclass models: ProjectRecord (core project metadata), DevPlanRecord/PhaseRecord/MilestoneRecord/BenchmarkRecord/ChecklistRecord/PerformanceMetricsRecord (project planning), DocumentSectionRecord/CustomTemplateRecord/DocumentChangeRecord/SyncStatusRecord/AgentReportCardRecord (Document Management 2.0), VectorIndexRecord/VectorShardMetadata (vector search). Models map directly to database tables with 1:1 correspondence. All use Python dataclasses with Optional fields for nullable columns and Dict[str, Any] for JSONB/JSON columns. Total 207 LOC with clear type annotations. | file=storage/models.py; loc=207; model_categories={\"core\": 1, \"document_mgmt\": 5, \"planning\": 6, \"vector\": 2}; models_count=13; reasoning={\"how\": \"Complete file read of models.py, analyzed each @dataclass decorator, mapped models to table schemas, categorized by functional domain\", \"what\": \"Cataloged all 13 dataclass models, their fields, types, default values, and relationships to database tables\", \"why\": \"Data models define the contract between storage backends and application code - must document structure for architecture understanding\"}; task=task_5_data_models; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T11:52:14.715624+00:00_5957ddbe", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T11:52:14.715660+00:00"}
