{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 11:52:56 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase2-Storage] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Task 6 (State Management) - State management architecture analyzed. Primary components: state/manager.py (334 LOC, StateManager class handling project state, recent tools, session tracking with atomic file writes and versioning), utils/rotation_state.py (528 LOC, RotationStateManager for log rotation sequence tracking with hash chains), 25+ JSON state files in state/ directory for rotation audit trails. StateManager uses file-based persistence (state.json) with asyncio locks, RotationStateManager uses threading.RLock. Both provide atomic write operations and corruption recovery. State is NOT stored in database, creating parallel persistence layer outside StorageBackend abstraction. | components={\"rotation_state\": \"utils/rotation_state.py\", \"state_manager\": \"state/manager.py\"}; critical_finding=state_not_in_database; loc_total=862; reasoning={\"how\": \"File analysis of manager.py and rotation_state.py, directory scanning for state files, architecture pattern identification\", \"what\": \"Documented StateManager (project state, sessions, tools history), RotationStateManager (rotation sequences, hash chains), JSON file-based persistence separate from database\", \"why\": \"State management is parallel persistence layer - must understand relationship to StorageBackend and identify integration gaps\"}; state_files_count=25; task=task_6_state_mgmt; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T11:52:56.351012+00:00_4aaf6075", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T11:52:56.351045+00:00"}
