{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-05 12:35:51 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase3-SysPath] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Research phase complete with full reasoning chain documentation - sys.path pattern audit establishes foundation for src/ migration | confidence=0.95; evidence_trail={\"context_inspection\": [\"server.py\", \"conftest.py\", \"scripts/*\"], \"files_analyzed\": 70, \"grep_pattern\": \"sys\\\\.path\\\\.(insert append)\", \"outliers_flagged\": 3}; phase=research; reasoning={\"how\": \"Methodology: ripgrep discovery -> manual categorization by context -> necessity analysis per occurrence -> quick win ROI calculation -> cross-team handoff identification. Uncertainty remaining: Whether server.py bootstrap can be eliminated (requires runtime testing), actual effort for standardization pre-migration (estimated 2-3 hours)\", \"what\": \"Constraints analyzed: package architecture (non-installable), test isolation requirements, script standalone execution, production bootstrap needs. Alternatives considered: conftest.py centralization (rejected - doesn't eliminate root cause), PYTHONPATH env var (rejected - fragile), editable install (requires src/ migration first). Coverage: 100% of Python files, 4 distinct pattern types documented\", \"why\": \"Understand complete sys.path landscape to identify: (1) immediate removal candidates, (2) migration blockers, (3) patterns requiring standardization before migration\"}; research_findings={\"dominant_pattern\": \"test parent.parent (93%)\", \"migration_impact\": \"65 test files affected\", \"production_concerns\": \"server.py bootstrap debatable\", \"quick_win_potential\": \"2-3 debug files (1 hour effort)\"}; team=A; total_log_entries=7; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.035684+00:00_0016e649", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.035720+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.035684+00:00_0016e649", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.045731+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-05 12:35:51 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase3-SrcMigration] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Team A sys.path analysis integrated: 70 occurrences total (65 tests, 5 scripts, 2 production). Key insight: 95.7% of sys.path hacks are REQUIRED under current architecture but will be ELIMINATED by src/ migration with pip install -e. This validates that src/ migration is the correct solution. | confidence=0.95; key_insight=src_migration_eliminates_syspath_hacks; phase=3; reasoning={\"how\": \"Analyzed Team A's pattern categorization: Test Pattern (78.6%), Script Pattern (7.1%), Production Bootstrap (1.4%). Migration impact: 65 test sys.path deletions immediate, 5 script deletions if using console_scripts entry points. This is strong ROI for migration.\", \"what\": \"Team A found 67 REQUIRED sys.path hacks (95.7%) that exist because scribe_mcp isn't properly packaged. Migration to src/scribe_mcp/ + pip install -e eliminates need for ALL test hacks (65 files) and most script hacks (5 files).\", \"why\": \"Need to validate that src/ migration actually solves the problems Team A identified - this is core justification for migration effort\"}; syspath_breakdown={\"debug\": 2, \"production\": 2, \"removable_percentage\": 95.7, \"scripts\": 5, \"tests\": 65, \"total\": 70}; task=team_a_analysis_integration; team=C; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.118019+00:00_0cbc90c9", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T12:35:51.118053+00:00"}
