{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 12:37:58 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase3-CircularDeps] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Analyzed lazy binding pattern #1 (tools \u2194 server): Tools import 'from scribe_mcp.server import app' at module level (lines 7-8) and use @app.tool() decorator (line 21) to register functions. Server imports 'from scribe_mcp import tools' at line 458 AFTER app is fully initialized. The tools/__init__.py imports all tool modules to trigger registration. This is a plugin registration pattern - acceptable and intentional. | acceptable=True; confidence=1; evidence_files=[\"server.py:458\", \"tools/__init__.py:3-17\", \"tools/health_check.py:8,21\"]; pattern=plugin_registration; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced import flow: server creates app \\u2192 tools import app \\u2192 tools use @app.tool() \\u2192 server imports tools (triggering registration). This is standard plugin architecture.\", \"what\": \"Tools need app decorator at module level. Server imports tools package after app is created. This ensures app exists before tools try to use @app.tool() decorator.\", \"why\": \"Need to understand if this pattern is MCP framework requirement or refactorable\"}; timing=import_after_initialization; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T12:37:58.680012+00:00_05f82632", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T12:37:58.680064+00:00"}
