{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 13:24:55 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase4-APIValidator] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Reading coordination file and establishing scope boundaries - Team D owns API signature/behavior validation, return type verification, parameter validation, Phase 3 YAML spec validation, error documentation, edge case behavior. Does NOT find dead code (Team A) or design new APIs (Phase 6). | coordination_file=wiki/analysis/phase_4_coordination.md; expected_overlaps=[\"dead_apis_to_team_a\", \"legacy_apis_from_team_c\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read phase_4_coordination.md lines 91-125 establishing boundaries. Confirmed expected overlaps: may discover dead APIs (handoff to Team A), may find undocumented legacy APIs (coordinate with Team C). Will use meta={'handoff_to': 'Team X'} for out-of-scope findings.\", \"what\": \"Team D scope: 28 tool APIs, behavior verification (not just signatures), return types, parameters, YAML specs, exceptions, edge cases. Cross-references: Phase 1 wikis (28 tools), Phase 2 storage docs, Phase 3 YAML specs, Team C legacy findings (deprecated APIs).\", \"why\": \"Must establish clear scope boundaries to prevent overlap with Teams A (dead code), B (duplication), C (legacy), E (cross-validation). Coordination file prevents duplicate work across parallel agents.\"}; scope_boundaries_confirmed=True; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T13:24:55.317165+00:00_bcefe1be", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T13:24:55.317195+00:00"}
