{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 13:27:04 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase4-Duplication] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Config object duplication analyzed - found 95% structural similarity across 3 config classes (AppendEntryConfig: 590 LOC, QueryEntriesConfig: 590 LOC, RotateLogConfig: 494 LOC = 1674 total LOC). Shared patterns: validation infrastructure, normalization methods, Phase 1 utility imports, __post_init__ pattern, dataclass structure | confidence=0.92; consolidation_target=[BUCKET:config]; duplication_id=DUPLICATION-003; loc_total=1674; phase=4; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read all three config files in tools/config/. Identified shared patterns: dataclass decorators, field() defaults, _validator/_config_manager fields, validation error collection, parameter normalization. Estimated 200-300 LOC could be extracted to BaseToolConfig with inheritance\", \"what\": \"AppendEntryConfig (590 LOC), QueryEntriesConfig (590 LOC), RotateLogConfig (494 LOC) all implement: Phase 1 utility imports (ToolValidator, ConfigManager, ErrorHandler), __post_init__ validation, normalize() methods, validate() methods, list parameter normalization, enum validation patterns\", \"why\": \"Three separate config classes implement nearly identical validation/normalization infrastructure - massive opportunity for base class extraction\"}; similarity_score=0.95; stage=research; team=B; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T13:27:04.714130+00:00_1f89338e", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T13:27:04.714165+00:00"}
