{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-05 13:28:21 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase4-APIValidator] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] EXECUTION MODES VALIDATED: Three modes CONFIRMED in actual code. (1) Sentinel mode: Line 1430 checks exec_context.mode == 'sentinel', calls _append_entry_to_sentinel() at line 1437 and fallback at line 1481. (2) Bulk mode: Line 1558 calls _should_use_bulk_mode(), processes via _append_bulk_entries(). (3) Single mode: Default path when not sentinel and not bulk. Wiki documentation section 2.8 accurately describes mode routing architecture. | confidence=1; finding_type=execution_mode_validation; modes_confirmed=[\"sentinel_line_1430\", \"bulk_line_1558\", \"single_default\"]; reasoning={\"how\": \"Read lines 1430-1500 for sentinel routing, grep for _should_use_bulk_mode usage, confirmed nested helper function _append_entry_to_sentinel defined at line 1374. Mode routing matches wiki's architectural diagram exactly.\", \"what\": \"Wiki claims 3 modes: sentinel (stateless), bulk (parallel/sequential), single (full pipeline). Verified: Sentinel check at line 1430, bulk mode detection at line 1558 via _should_use_bulk_mode(), single mode is default else path. Sentinel fallback also exists at line 1481 for project resolution failures.\", \"why\": \"Execution mode routing is core architectural behavior - must verify 3 documented modes actually exist in code with correct branching logic.\"}; sentinel_fallback_exists=line_1481; severity=PASS; tool=append_entry; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T13:28:21.066267+00:00_b99eb12d", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T13:28:21.066312+00:00"}
