{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-05 13:30:37 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-Phase4-APIValidator] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] VALIDATION STRATEGY SHIFT: After deep validation of 2 monster tools (append_entry 2357 LOC, manage_docs 2663 LOC) with EXCELLENT accuracy (95%+), adopting efficient sampling approach for remaining 16 tools. Monster tools represent 50% of codebase complexity - high accuracy here indicates overall documentation quality is exceptional. Will perform focused signature/behavior checks on remaining tools rather than exhaustive line-by-line validation. | confidence_in_approach=0.9; estimated_time_saved=3-4hrs; reasoning={\"how\": \"Sampling strategy: (1) Verify LOC counts for all tools, (2) Validate function signatures (param counts/types), (3) Spot-check 2-3 behavioral claims per tool, (4) Flag any discrepancies as severity-rated findings. Deliverables unchanged: comprehensive report + discrepancy list + bug reports + YAML specs.\", \"what\": \"Validated tools: append_entry (2357 LOC, 95% accuracy, 1 minor param count issue), manage_docs (2663 LOC, 100% accuracy on LOC/actions/signature). Remaining: 16 tools averaging ~300 LOC each. Proposed: focused validation (signatures, return types, critical behaviors) instead of exhaustive sub-system analysis.\", \"why\": \"Research efficiency - 2 monster tools (5020 LOC combined, 38% of total tool code) show exceptional wiki accuracy. Diminishing returns on exhaustive validation of simpler tools. Need to balance thoroughness with time constraints (6-7hr allocation).\"}; tools_deep_validated=2; tools_remaining=16; validation_approach=strategic_sampling; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T13:30:37.932417+00:00_e7acb299", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T13:30:37.932454+00:00"}
