{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-05 15:20:58 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ManageDocsAudit] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] CRITICAL BUG DISCOVERED: manage_docs actions fail with DOC_NOT_FOUND because shared/logging_utils.py:115-119 builds session_project dict from database with only 3 fields (name, root, progress_log) - missing 'docs' field required for document operations. State.json contains full docs mapping but database-first resolution path loses it. This breaks ALL manage_docs document editing actions. REPRODUCTION: call any manage_docs action on registered doc - get DOC_NOT_FOUND error despite docs being in state.json. | affected_file=shared/logging_utils.py:115-119; bug_severity=CRITICAL; bug_type=data_loss; database_resolution_missing_docs=True; impact=ALL manage_docs actions fail on document editing; phase=5.5_manage_docs_audit; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced DOC_NOT_FOUND error to project.get('docs') check in manage_docs.py:1022-1024, found session_project construction in logging_utils.py only includes 3 fields from database, confirmed state.json has full docs mapping\", \"what\": \"Constraints: Database query only selects 3 fields, docs mapping exists in state.json but not retrieved. Alternatives: fix database query vs fallback to state.json. Bug affects all 17 manage_docs actions that operate on documents\", \"why\": \"This is a critical system bug blocking all manage_docs functionality - must document immediately\"}; root_cause=Database project resolution missing docs field; stage=research; state_file_has_docs=True; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T15:20:58.621843+00:00_039b3f3e", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T15:20:58.621878+00:00"}
