{"op": "append", "content": "[\u274c] [2026-01-05 15:23:39 UTC] [Agent: ResearchAgent-ManageDocsAudit] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED: scribe_projects database table schema is MISSING docs_json column entirely! Table only has: id, name, repo_root, progress_log_path, created_at, updated_at, status, phase, confidence, completed_at, last_activity, description, last_entry_at, last_access_at, last_status_change, tags, meta. NO docs_json field exists. This is why shared/logging_utils.py can't SELECT it. FIX REQUIRED: (1) ALTER TABLE to add docs_json TEXT column, (2) UPDATE existing projects to populate from state.json, (3) Modify set_project to INSERT/UPDATE docs_json, (4) Update logging_utils.py query to SELECT and JSON-parse docs_json into project['docs']. | columns_found=16; fix_components=4; fix_steps=[\"ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN docs_json TEXT\", \"UPDATE existing rows from state.json\", \"Modify set_project tool to populate docs_json\", \"Update logging_utils.py SELECT query\"]; missing_column=docs_json; phase=5.5_manage_docs_audit; reasoning={\"how\": \"Queried scribe_projects table schema with PRAGMA table_info, confirmed docs_json column does not exist, traced back to logging_utils.py query failure\", \"what\": \"Constraints: Database schema incomplete, 16 columns but missing docs. Alternatives: add column vs restructure schema vs fallback to state.json. Chose add column for minimal disruption\", \"why\": \"Must identify complete root cause and fix requirements for implementation team\"}; root_cause=database_schema_missing_docs_json_column; stage=research; table=scribe_projects; priority=high; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-05T15:23:39.868248+00:00_3783f5d5", "timestamp": "2026-01-05T15:23:39.868280+00:00"}
