{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2139\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 22:00:07 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-SchemaFix] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Investigation finding: Tools appear to be auto-registered from tools/ directory. The _tool_decorator in server.py (lines 142-169) creates MCP tool schemas with additionalProperties=True by default, which should allow all parameters. Need to check how manage_docs is actually being called and if there's explicit schema override. | finding=auto_registration; issue=default schema uses additionalProperties true but may have explicit override; location=server.py:142-169; priority=low; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T22:00:07.834564+00:00_4ee1eaa2", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T22:00:07.834595+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T22:00:07.834564+00:00_4ee1eaa2", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T22:00:07.845181+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-07 22:00:43 UTC] [Agent: CoderAgent-SchemaFix] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Key finding: All tools use @app.tool() without explicit input_schema. The _tool_decorator in server.py defaults to {\"type\": \"object\", \"properties\": {}, \"additionalProperties\": true}. This means MCP SDK may not be introspecting Python function signatures to expose parameters. The issue is that parameters exist in Python but aren't exposed in the MCP tool schema that clients see. | implication=MCP clients don't know about edit, doc_name, or batch special handling; location=server.py:152-156; root_cause=default_schema_too_generic; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-07T22:00:43.479959+00:00_ff08669f", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T22:00:43.479991+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-07T22:00:43.479959+00:00_ff08669f", "timestamp": "2026-01-07T22:00:43.489926+00:00"}
