{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-08 01:17:02 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Test revealed critical issue with fix: set_project creates PROGRESS_LOG.md file BEFORE state detection, so even genuinely new projects have log files and are incorrectly treated as EXISTING. Need to rethink approach - perhaps check database/state instead of file existence. | value={\"bug_discovery\": \"fix_breaks_new_projects\", \"root_cause\": \"set_project creates log file before state detection\", \"reasoning\": {\"why\": \"File existence check fails because set_project creates files during initialization\", \"what\": \"Log file exists even for NEW projects because it's created early in set_project flow\", \"how\": \"Need alternative approach - check database/state for previous project usage, not file existence\"}}}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T01:17:02.625041+00:00_f1dc986f", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:17:02.625075+00:00"}
