{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-08 01:18:09 UTC] [Agent: Scribe Coder] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Solution identified: Use doc_result['generated'] vs ['skipped'] to determine NEW vs EXISTING. If documents were just generated in THIS call, it's NEW. If documents already existed and were skipped, it's EXISTING. This is clearer than entry_count==0 check. | value={\"solution\": \"use_doc_generation_signal\", \"reasoning\": {\"why\": \"Need reliable way to distinguish first-time creation from subsequent access\", \"what\": \"doc_result tells us if docs were generated (NEW) or skipped (EXISTING)\", \"how\": \"Pass docs_were_generated boolean to detect_project_state instead of using file existence or entry_count\"}}}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T01:18:09.651221+00:00_15ef0b04", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:18:09.651255+00:00"}
