{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-08 01:22:31 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent-Stage5-Audit1] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] SPEC-SET-001 Review: Empty Log Detection Fix - Tests PASSED (2/2) with warnings. Implementation correctly uses docs_were_generated flag instead of entry_count==0. Logic flow verified: docs created \u2192 NEW, docs existed \u2192 EXISTING_LEGACY. However, runtime warnings detected: unawaited coroutines in logging_utils.py (check_reminder_cooldown, record_reminder_shown). This is a pre-existing issue outside SPEC-SET-001 scope but should be noted. | issue_found=unawaited_coroutines_in_logging_utils; issue_scope=pre_existing_not_spec_related; reasoning={\"how\": \"Ran pytest with -v flag, inspected code flow in project_utils.py and set_project.py, confirmed docs_were_generated derived from doc_result['files'] length\", \"what\": \"Tests pass, logic correct (docs_were_generated flag properly integrated), but warnings indicate potential async handling issues in logging_utils\", \"why\": \"Verify empty log detection bug fix correctly distinguishes NEW vs EXISTING projects after rotation\"}; spec=SPEC-SET-001; tests_failed=0; tests_passed=2; warnings=5; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T01:22:31.486029+00:00_38bf65e2", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:22:31.486065+00:00"}
