{"op": "append", "content": "[\u26a0\ufe0f] [2026-01-08 01:25:02 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent-Stage5-Audit1] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] SPEC-SET-001 DEEP ANALYSIS: Edge case review - POTENTIAL ISSUE IDENTIFIED. The implementation uses `docs_were_generated = len(doc_result.get(\"files\", [])) > 0`. However, if generate_doc_templates skips all docs (already exist), files list is empty even though project exists. Need to verify this edge case doesn't break detection. Also noted: progress_log_path parameter added but marked unused - could be removed for cleaner API but kept for backwards compatibility. Overall logic sound but edge case warrants validation. | analysis_type=edge_case_review; potential_issue=docs_were_generated_when_all_skipped; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced logic flow: docs skipped \\u2192 files=[] \\u2192 docs_were_generated=False \\u2192 EXISTING_LEGACY - this is actually CORRECT for the use case\", \"what\": \"If all docs skipped (project re-activation), files=[] makes docs_were_generated=False which is CORRECT behavior - project should show EXISTING not NEW\", \"why\": \"Deep adversarial review requires edge case analysis beyond happy path testing\"}; requires_validation=True; severity=low; spec=SPEC-SET-001; unused_parameter=progress_log_path; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T01:25:02.183507+00:00_eeba878d", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:25:02.183538+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-08T01:25:02.183507+00:00_eeba878d", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:25:02.193510+00:00"}
{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-08 01:25:18 UTC] [Agent: ReviewAgent-Stage5-Audit1] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] SPEC-SET-001 EDGE CASE RESOLUTION: After deeper analysis, the edge case is actually CORRECTLY handled. When re-activating existing project: docs skipped \u2192 files=[] \u2192 docs_were_generated=False \u2192 detect_project_state() returns EXISTING_LEGACY. This is the INTENDED behavior - we want existing projects to show EXISTING, not NEW. The test test_bug_001_empty_log_shows_existing_sitrep validates exactly this scenario. Edge case concern WITHDRAWN - implementation is sound. | analysis_type=edge_case_resolution; edge_case=project_reactivation_with_skipped_docs; reasoning={\"how\": \"Traced complete flow through test case: create project \\u2192 rotate \\u2192 re-activate \\u2192 verify EXISTING message appears\", \"what\": \"Re-activation scenario correctly returns EXISTING when docs_were_generated=False - test validates this exact flow\", \"why\": \"Must verify edge case doesn't break functionality before finalizing grade\"}; spec=SPEC-SET-001; test_coverage=test_bug_001_empty_log_shows_existing_sitrep; verdict=correctly_handled; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T01:25:18.933633+00:00_4bd8da12", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T01:25:18.933667+00:00"}
