{"op": "append", "content": "[\u2705] [2026-01-08 02:45:52 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] Documented `apply_patch` action comprehensively in SKILL.md - the PRIMARY method for editing managed docs. Tested and verified all modes work:  **Structured Mode (default)** - Uses `edit` parameter: 1. `replace_range` - Line-based (start_line, end_line, content) 2. `replace_section` - Section ID-based (section, content) 3. `replace_block` - Anchor-based (anchor, new_content) - replaces from anchor to blank line  **Unified Mode** - Uses `patch` + `patch_mode=\"unified\"` for standard diff format  Added workflow guidance: always dry_run first, get line numbers via read_file search mode, or get section IDs via list_sections. | changes=[\"Added 'apply_patch - THE PRIMARY EDITING METHOD' section at line 366\", \"Updated 'Common Mistakes to Avoid' with correct apply_patch guidance\"]; file=.codex/skills/scribe-mcp-usage/SKILL.md; reasoning={\"how\": \"Verified each mode with dry_run tests, added comprehensive usage guide\", \"what\": \"Tested all 4 edit modes, documented schemas and workflow\", \"why\": \"User requested detailed apply_patch documentation as it will be the MAIN editing method\"}; priority=medium; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T02:45:52.283945+00:00_07fc593e", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T02:45:52.283980+00:00"}
