{"op": "append", "content": "[\ud83e\udded] [2026-01-08 04:52:23 UTC] [Agent: Orchestrator] [Project: scribe_systematic_audit_1] CRITICAL DECISION: Standardize manage_docs parameters to use doc_name and doc_category  ## Problem Identified The `doc` parameter in manage_docs has conflated semantics: - For EDIT actions: means document KEY/NAME (e.g., \"architecture\", \"checklist\") - references registered docs - For CREATE actions: was meant to be CATEGORY (e.g., \"research\", \"bugs\", \"wiki\") - Auto-registration code uses it as doc NAME, not category - This caused confusion and incorrect parameter naming during refactor attempt  ## Decision Standardize on TWO distinct parameters: 1. `doc_name` - The specific document identifier/key (for edits, auto-registration) 2. `doc_category` - The document category/type (for create actions, routing)  ## Rationale - Clear semantic separation between \"which doc\" vs \"what type of doc\" - Eliminates the confusing dual-use of single `doc` param - Makes API self-documenting - Aligns with existing `doc_name` usage in create_research_doc  ## Implementation Required - Rename `doc` param t... | category=architecture_decision; component=manage_docs; priority=medium; reasoning={\"how\": \"systematic rename with clear semantic boundaries\", \"what\": \"standardize on doc_name + doc_category separation\", \"why\": \"doc param has confusing dual semantics causing implementation errors\"}; log_type=progress; content_type=log\n", "file_path": "/home/austin/projects/MCP_SPINE/scribe_mcp/.scribe/docs/dev_plans/scribe_systematic_audit_1/PROGRESS_LOG.md", "id": "2026-01-08T04:52:23.884038+00:00_83addc1a", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T04:52:23.884069+00:00"}
{"op": "commit", "ref_id": "2026-01-08T04:52:23.884038+00:00_83addc1a", "timestamp": "2026-01-08T04:52:23.894472+00:00"}
